+# Definition of Done
+
+> Today `chatOrchestrator` calls `afterModelResponse` once after the tool loop exits and hands it `lastUsage` — the usage from the final round only (`src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` line 125). In a turn that ran two tool rounds before the final answer, the provider was called three times and billed for three calls, and the hook sees the tokens of one of them. Any cost or audit record built on `afterModelResponse` silently under-counts every turn that used a tool.
+
+**Strategy: `direct`** — `createChatOrchestrator` and `OrchestratorHooks.afterModelResponse` already exist and can be driven through `processMessage` with a multi-round tool-calling provider today; the test fails on behaviour because `chatOrchestrator` overwrites `lastUsage` on each round instead of summing `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` across rounds.
+
+## Done when these pass
+
+- [ ] **sums inputTokens, outputTokens, and totalTokens across every provider round of a multi-round tool turn** — runs a 3-round tool turn where round 1 reports `{inputTokens: 100, outputTokens: 25, totalTokens: 125}`, round 2 omits usage, and round 3 reports `{inputTokens: 160, outputTokens: 40, totalTokens: 200}`, and asserts `afterModelResponse` receives `{inputTokens: 260, outputTokens: 65, totalTokens: 325}`. Fails today because `lastUsage` is overwritten rather than accumulated, so `afterModelResponse` receives `{inputTokens: 160, outputTokens: 40, totalTokens: 200}` (only the final round).
+      `src/orchestration/toolRoundUsage.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+## Facets
+
+- [ ] Sum `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` across every provider round that reported `UsageMetadata` in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` before passing usage to `afterModelResponse`.
+- [ ] Keep `usage` as `undefined` when no round in the turn reports usage, and preserve single-round behaviour where the single round's `UsageMetadata` is passed unchanged.
+- [ ] Add unit tests in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts` covering single-round, all-`undefined` multi-round, and mixed-round usage, and add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry noting that `afterModelResponse` now receives summed usage across tool rounds.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Automatically wiring `UsageStore` into the orchestrator.
+- Adding a per-round hook or changing `MessageChunk` on the stream (each round's `stop` chunk still carries its own round's `usage`).
+- Pricing or cost calculation beyond `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens`.
